-  (`[EXC-17]`), and the fields of a `@sync` class need none (`[THR-1]`).
+  and marks nothing again. An access is **held** when code other than the access itself runs between
+  its beginning and its end. An access that is not held — no code of the program runs while it is
+  active and no other access begins inside it, as for `len(h.items)` or `h.items.push(x)` — is checked
+  but not counted, since nothing could observe the count. So is the whole-object write of a `mut self`
+  call to a **quiet** function: one that begins no access, drops nothing whose drop runs code of the
+  program, and calls only built-ins that call no code back and other quiet functions. The cost is one
+  word per non-`Copy` field, plus a zero word for a class whose own count is odd; at most one check
+  per such field on entry to a `mut self` method; and, per access, a load and a compare, with a store
+  only for a held access. `Copy` fields have no word (`[EXC-17]`), and the fields of a `@sync` class
+  need none (`[THR-1]`).
